  "codebook": {
    "definition": "Credit-claiming occurs when a senator explicitly attributes a positive outcome, action, or achievement to their own efforts, role, or advocacy, thereby seeking recognition or responsibility for the result.",
    "clarification": "Credit-claiming is identified when the senator uses first-person language (e.g., 'I secured,' 'I authored,' 'I announced') or explicitly links their actions to a tangible benefit, funding allocation, legislative success, or recognition. It often involves highlighting their personal or leadership role in achieving a specific outcome for their constituents, state, or a broader cause.",
    "positive_examples": [
      {
        "text": "Sen. Byron Dorgan (D-ND) announced Friday that U.S. Energy Secretary Samuel Bodman has officially designated Bismarck State College (BSC) as the National Power Plant Operations Technology and Educational Center. Dorgan said the designation is a recognition of the school's cutting-edge education and training program. This designation will help attract students, industry, and federal funding to help carry out BSC's mission. Dorgan authored legislation, which was signed into law, that created the National Center designation.",
        "explanation": "Senator Dorgan explicitly takes credit for authoring the legislation that led to the designation of Bismarck State College as a National Center, directly linking his legislative efforts to the outcome."
      },
      {
        "text": "Sen. Jim Talent (R-Mo.) today announced that the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) has declared most of Missouri a disaster area due to the severe drought. Sen. Talent and USDA Undersecretary Bill Hawks will make a formal announcement tomorrow morning following a roundtable discussion with producer leaders in St. Louis. The disaster designation, requested by Missouri Gov. Matt Blunt, will make all qualified farm operators eligible for low-interest emergency (EM) loans from USDA's Farm Service Agency (FSA). 'We are doing everything we can to help Missouri farmers and ranchers cope with one of the driest growing seasons in recent memory,' said Sen. Talent, who worked with USDA officials to expedite the approval of the Governor's request.",
        "explanation": "Senator Talent explicitly states that he worked with USDA officials to expedite the approval of the disaster designation, taking personal credit for securing assistance for Missouri farmers."
      },
      {
        "text": "U.S. Senator Charles E. Schumer today announced that Westchester County has received two federal grants totaling $134,004 from the 2006 Assistance to Firefighters Grant (AFG) Program administered by the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS). 'This funding will go a long way in supporting the first responders in Westchester County,' said Schumer. 'We can never truly repay our firefighters and first responders for their heroic efforts and dedication to duty. However, we can ensure that they have the training, equipment, and resources they need to do their job well.' Schumer was among the first senators who recognized the need for the federal government to establish a funding program for local governments and fire departments to help defray the rising costs of equipment and fire prevention.",
        "explanation": "Senator Schumer explicitly announces the federal grants and takes credit for his role in advocating for and securing the funding, as well as his early recognition of the need for such a program."
      }
    ],
    "negative_clarification": "Credit-claiming does NOT occur when a senator discusses general policies, expresses opinions, criticizes others, or provides information without explicitly linking their own actions to a specific positive outcome. It also does not include routine announcements or statements that do not attribute the outcome to their personal efforts.",
    "negative_examples": [
      {
        "text": "Senator John Ensign made the following statement after the confirmation by the United States Senate of Michael Chertoff as Secretary of Homeland Security: 'Judge Chertoff comes to this position with a great deal of experience in law enforcement, counterterrorism, and management. He has dedicated his life to public service and understands the challenges we face in keeping our nation safe. I look forward to working with Judge Chertoff to ensure the security of Nevadans and all Americans.'",
        "explanation": "The senator expresses support for the confirmation but does not claim personal credit for any action or outcome. The statement is informational and does not link the senator's efforts to a specific achievement."
      },
      {
        "text": "The Senate late yesterday approved a resolution honoring the life and legacy of Senator Thomas F. Eagleton of Missouri. The resolution, introduced by Senators Harry Reid, Claire McCaskill, Mitch McConnell, Kit Bond, and others, passed unanimously. 'This resolution pays tribute to a man who was a statesman, an intellectual, and a man of the people all at once, and I'm so proud that we're honoring him with this resolution,' McCaskill said.",
        "explanation": "The senator discusses the passage of a resolution honoring someone else but does not claim personal credit for any specific action or achievement of their own."
      },
      {
        "text": "Today we remember the brave Americans who lost their lives 65 years ago during the attacks on Pearl Harbor. Each year on December 7, we are reminded of the price our military men and women have paid to protect us and our freedoms. We honor the brave Americans who have answered this call and those who serve so honorably today. We are deeply grateful for their service.",
        "explanation": "The text is a commemorative statement that honors others but does not involve the senator claiming credit for any personal action or achievement."
      }
    ]
  }
}
